lean-markupsafe is a clean-room reimplementation in Lean 4 of MarkupSafe
(https://github.com/pallets/markupsafe), which is licensed under BSD-3-Clause and remains the copyright of
its authors.

No source code from the upstream project is copied here. Its test suite and
documentation are used as the behavioural specification, and each
conformance case in tests/Conformance.lean names the upstream test it
re-expresses. docs/traceability.toml records the upstream commit this port
was read against.

LeanMarkupsafe/RepoImpl/Entities.lean is generated data: the WHATWG HTML
named character reference table (https://html.spec.whatwg.org/entities.json),
as distributed in CPython's html.entities.html5, which upstream's
Markup.unescape uses through html.unescape. The invalid numeric reference
tables in RepoImpl/Unescape.lean come from the same WHATWG specification.
